From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aayush Misra <aayushm@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2026 11:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Restrict the multilib set to 32-bit variants

"Support of multilibs with m64" and "-Added double arith instructions" add
m64 to MULTILIB_OPTIONS and then prune the unwanted combinations with
MULTILIB_EXCEPTIONS.  Those patterns are end-anchored, so combinations that
do not end in an m64 component - m64/le and m64/bs/le, for example - survive
and are requested by libgcc and newlib.

Apply this patch for a 32-bit-only toolchain.  It excludes every multilib
whose path starts with m64, leaving the twelve 32-bit variants, and it means
the MB-64 patches present in the tree contribute no installed libraries.
Leave it out to build all eighteen multilibs, which additionally needs the
MB-64 binutils support and the MB-64 fixes under mb64/fixes/.

Signed-off-by: Aayush Misra <aayushm@amd.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze b/gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze
--- a/gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze
+++ b/gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze
@@ -12,6 +12,12 @@ MULTILIB_EXCEPTIONS += *mxl-barrel-shift/mxl-multiply-high mxl-multiply-high
 MULTILIB_EXCEPTIONS += *mlittle-endian/mxl-multiply-high mxl-multiply-high
 MULTILIB_EXCEPTIONS += *m64/mxl-barrel-shift/mlittle-endian/mxl-multiply-high
 
+# The patterns above are end-anchored, so m64 combinations ending in
+# mlittle-endian survive and get requested by libgcc/newlib.  This build
+# targets 32-bit MicroBlaze only, so drop every m64 variant and leave the
+# twelve 32-bit multilibs.
+MULTILIB_EXCEPTIONS += m64*
+
 # Extra files
 microblaze-c.o: $(srcdir)/config/microblaze/microblaze-c.cc \
     $(srcdir)/config/microblaze/microblaze-protos.h \
